<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#papermaking">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Papermaking</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as paper-making</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Papermaking is the craft of producing paper from plant fibres, invented in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. According to a widely repeated tradition, Chinese prisoners taken at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas">Battle of Talas</a> in 751, a defeat for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, transmitted the technique westwards. Paper subsequently spread through the Islamic world and into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p></div>
